There was a woman from Canaan who lived near Sidon and Tyre. She came to him and fell down, weeping. And she said to him, "Lord, son of David! Have mercy on me!" For she was a woman whose daughter had an unclean spirit. And she was worn out by many things.
He didn't say a single word. Here are the students who answered. They said to him: "Get this away from us. Don't leave us alone in our state and she is screaming at us."
Jesus answered, "I was sent only to the lost sheep of Israel."
Then the woman fell to the ground in front of him. "Oh God! Help me!" she said.
Answer: "It is not right to take the children's bread and throw it to the dogs."
"Ah, my lord," she said. "But even dogs eat the scraps that fall from their master's table."
Then Jesus answered and said to her, "Woman, great is your faith! Let it be to you as you desire." And her daughter was healed at that moment. Jesus feeds the four thousand.
Jesus came out of there. He walked along the Sea of Galilee. Then he went up on a mountain and sat down.
Large crowds came to him. They brought blind people and lame people. They also brought those who were disabled, mute, and many others. They laid them at his feet, and he healed them.
The people were amazed. Those who didn't speak began to speak. Those who were paralyzed were healed. Those who couldn't walk began to walk. Those who were blind began to see. Thus, the people praised the God of Israel.
Then Jesus called his disciples to come to him. He said, "I am concerned about these people. They have been with me for three days and do not have anything to eat. I do not want to send them away hungry. If I do, they will collapse on the way home."
His disciples answered him, "There is nothing here." And they said to him, "Where will we get bread to satisfy so great a crowd?"
"Who has bread?" Jesus asked. "Seven loaves," they answered Him, "and a few small fish."
Jesus said to the multitudes, "Sit down on the ground."
I took seven loaves of bread and a fish, and gave thanks to my Lord. After he had given them a blessing, he sent them out to the disciples. And the disciples distributed them to the people.
All of them ate and were satisfied. After that, the disciples gathered seven baskets of leftovers.
The number of men who ate was 4,000. The women and children ate a lot.
And after Jesus had dispersed the crowd, he embarked on the boat. He walked to the place near Magdala.
They ask Jesus about an apparent miracle.
The Sadducees and Pharisees came to test Jesus. They asked him to show them a sign from heaven.
Answer: "At night you see the sky. You say, 'The weather tomorrow will be good. The sky is red.'"
And in the morning she says, "Today there will be a storm. The sky is red and cloudy." She knows what she sees in the sky means. But you cannot understand the signs of what is happening now.
A malicious and unfaithful people seek a divine sign. And you should not give them a sign except the sign of Jonah." Then Jesus left them and went away. The yeast of the Pharisees and Sadducees.
The pupils crossed over to the other side of the lake. They forgot to bring any bread with them.
"Beware," that's what Jesus told them. "Beware of the yeast of the Pharisees and Sadducees."
The students talked to each other because we didn't bring bread with us.
He knew what Jesus was going to say. So he said to them, "You have little faith! Why are you talking to each other about the bread?"
Haven't you understood until now? Don't you mention the five loaves for the five thousand? Don't you mention how much you gathered of baskets of fragments?
You do not remember the seven loaves for the four thousand? Do you not remember how many baskets you gathered up of fragments?
How did you not understand? I didn't talk to you about bread. But beware of the yeast of the Sadducees and Pharisees.
Then the disciples understood that Jesus was not warning them about bread yeast. He was warning them about the teachings of the Pharisees and Sadducees. Peter says that Jesus is the Christ.
Jesus went to the area of Caesarea Philippi. There he asked his disciples, "Who do people say the Son of Man is?"
They answered: "Some people say he is John the Baptist. Others say he is the prophet Elijah. Still others say he is the prophet Jeremiah, or one of the prophets."
"And who are you to say that I am?" he asked.
Simon Peter answered and said, "You are the Christ, the Son of the living God."
Jesus said to him, "Blessed are you, Simon son of Jonah! For it is not flesh and blood that has revealed this to you, but my Father who is in heaven."
This is what I tell you. You are Peter. On this rock I will build my church. The gates of hell will not prevail against it.
I give you the keys of the kingdom of heaven. What you bind on earth will be bound in heaven. And what you loose on earth will be loosed in heaven.
Jesus warned his disciples not to tell anyone that he is the Christ. Jesus speaks about his coming death.
From that moment, Jesus began to explain to his disciples what was going to happen to him. He told them he had to go to Jerusalem. There he would have to suffer at the hands of the chief priests, elders, and teachers. They would have him killed and he would rise from the dead on the third day.
"Master, let this cup pass from me; nevertheless, not as I will, but as You will." And He said to Peter, "Get behind Me, Satan! You are an offense to Me, for you are not mindful of the things that are of God, but those things which are of men."
Jesus turned and said to Peter, "Get behind me, Satan! You are a stumbling block to me; for you are not setting your mind on the things of God, but on the things of men."
Then Jesus spoke to his disciples. He said to them, "If anyone wants to become my follower, he must deny himself and take up his cross and follow me."
If he wants to save his soul, he will lose it. But if he loses his soul for me, he will find it.
Why would someone gain the whole world and lose themselves? Or what could possibly change about oneself?
"The son of man is coming in the glory of his Father. His angels will come with him, and he will give to everyone according to their deeds."
What I am going to tell you is true. Some of the people standing here will not die before they see the Son of Man coming in his Kingdom."
Jesus Christ's Appearance Changes.
And after six days, He took Jesus with Him, along with Peter, James, and John, the brother of James. And He brought them up to a high mountain. And they were all alone by themselves.
Hani, in front of them, his appearance changed. His face was shining like the sun. His clothes became white like the light.
Suddenly, Moses and Elijah appeared before them. Moses and Elijah were talking with Jesus.
Peter said to Jesus, "Lord, it is better for us to be here. If you wish, I will put up three tents. One for you, one for Moses, and one for Elijah."
When Peter was just barely old enough to speak, even then a cloud of disapproval surrounded him. He heard a voice from the cloud saying, "This is my son, whom I love. I am very pleased with him. Listen to him!"
When the disciples heard these words, they were terrified. They fell face down on the ground.
But Jesus came and touched them. He said to them, "Arise, and do not be afraid."
When they raised their eyes, they saw only Jesus.
They came down from the mountain. On their way, Jesus told them what they must do. "Do not tell anyone what you have seen," he said to them. "Wait until the Son of Man is raised from the dead."
The students asked him, "Why do the teachers say that Elias must come first?"
Jesus answered, "It is true. Elijah must come and make everything new again."
But we tell you, if she comes and people do not recognize her, they will do everything they want to do to her. "That is how they will treat the child of others."
Then the disciples understood that Jesus was speaking to them about John the Baptist. Jesus heals a boy who was possessed by a demon.
When they came near the crowd, a man went up to Jesus Christ. He knelt down before him.
He said, "O my lord, have mercy on my son. He is shaking violently and suffering greatly. He falls down frequently into the fire or into the water."
I brought him to your disciples. But they were not able to heal him."
"O infidels and sons of bitches! Why do I have to stay with you? Why do I have to be patient with you? Bring me this boy."
Jesus said to the devil, "Come out of the boy," and he came out of him. He was healed at the same moment.
The disciples came to Jesus in private. And they asked him, "Why could we not drive out the demon?"
Answer: "What you have said is true, but your faith is too small. If you had faith even as small as a mustard seed, you could say to this mountain, 'Go, throw yourself into the sea,' and it would do it. Nothing would be impossible for you."
