They gathered in Galilee. Then Jesus told them, "The Son of Man is to be betrayed into the hands of men."
They will kill him. On the third day he will rise from among the dead." Then the disciples were filled with deep sorrow. Jesus pays the temple tax.
Jesus and his disciples arrived at Capernaum. Meanwhile, the tax collectors came to Peter. They said to him, "Does your teacher not pay the temple tax?"
"Yes, he does it that way," he answered. When Peter came into the house, Jesus began to speak. "What do you think, Simon?" they asked him. "The kings of the earth, who do they collect taxes and duties from? From their own sons or from other people?"
Peter answered him, "From others." Jesus said, "Thus the children are free."
But we don't want to anger them. Go to the lake and cast your line. Take the first fish you catch. Open its mouth. You will find the exact money you need inside. Take it and give it to those who owe taxes, you and I.
